NAME
     start-stop-daemon - start and stop daemons from a script

SYNOPSIS
     start-stop-daemon --start [--pidfile FILE] [--exec PATH] [--background]
                       [--make-pidfile] [--chuid USER] [--] [ARG...]
     start-stop-daemon --stop [--pidfile FILE] [--exec PATH]
                       [--signal SIG] [--retry N]

DESCRIPTION
     start-stop-daemon is what an init script uses to start a daemon
     once and to stop it again: it looks for a process matching the
     pidfile or the executable, and starts or signals accordingly. Its
     exit status says whether anything was done.

OPTIONS
     --start, --stop     which way round
     --pidfile FILE      where the process id is kept
     --exec PATH         match on this executable
     --background        put it in the background
     --make-pidfile      write the pidfile after starting
     --chuid USER        run as that user
     --signal SIG        the signal to send when stopping
     --retry N           wait N seconds, then use KILL

SEE ALSO
     service(8), init(8)
